cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this comparison registry or the evaluation protocol, cite it alongside the primary sources it aggregates (see data/references.csv)."
title: "Glass vs Plastic: a study of algorithms, models and sensors for material discrimination"
abstract: >-
  A comparison of 38 model families and sensor configurations for separating glass from plastic,
  scored on ten criteria with four weighting profiles, together with a reproducible classical-ML
  tier, an optional PyTorch/timm tier, a physics-based cue taxonomy, and an evaluation protocol
  including leakage controls and a statistical power analysis.
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-11
license: MIT
type: software
keywords:
  - material classification
  - waste sorting
  - recycling
  - glass
  - plastic
  - computer vision
  - hyperspectral imaging
  - evaluation protocol
